      "id": "radar-record-order",
      "name": "Radar: record order",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        -380,
        -20
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "name": "Radar Orders Key"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Records the order in the Buyer Radar: one order row, the buyer won in the lead register, and the owner told on WhatsApp (or by email when Meta refuses). A reference already recorded answers 200 with duplicate:true and changes nothing."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Google Sheets: two minutes, then the register copies itself\n\nThe **Register order in Google Sheets** node is fully configured - appendOrUpdate,\nkeyed on `order_id`, all fourteen columns mapped. The only thing missing is a\nGoogle credential, because this n8n has none.\n\n1. Left sidebar -> **Credentials** -> **Add credential** -> search **Google Sheets**\n   -> choose **Google Sheets OAuth2 API** (or **Google Service Account**) -> sign in\n   with the Google account that owns the register, and save it.\n2. Open this workflow -> click **Register order in Google Sheets** -> pick that\n   credential in **Credential to connect with**.\n3. Give it the spreadsheet: either set `ORDERS_SHEET_ID` (and optionally\n   `ORDERS_SHEET_NAME`, default `Orders`) in the n8n container environment, or\n   paste the spreadsheet id straight into **Document** on the node.\n4. **Save**. The next order appends a row; the same order twice updates that row.\n\nUntil then nothing is lost: the node continues on failure, so the radar still\nrecords every order, the buyer is still won in the lead register, and the owner is\nstill told. Only the sheet copy is missing.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "note-sheets-setup",
      "name": "Google Sheets Setup Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -120,
        -680
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The owner is told by the radar, not from here\n\nThe placeholder WhatsApp node is gone. **Radar: record order** posts the order to\nthe Buyer Radar, which records it, puts the buyer in the lead register as\n`won`, and sends the WhatsApp text to the owner from the number that is already\nconnected there - falling back to email when Meta refuses (error 131047, the closed\n24-hour window).\n\nThe buyer is never messaged by the radar.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 380
      },
      "id": "note-radar",
      "name": "Radar Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -540,
        -680
      ]
    }
